Different political systems mainly vary in where these functions are located and how feedback travels.

So monarchy vs democracy becomes only one dimension.

Other important axes include:

centralized ↔ distributed

fast decision ↔ deliberative decision

high coercion ↔ high consent

personal authority ↔ institutional authority

short feedback loops ↔ long feedback loops

local autonomy ↔ standardized control

That explains why two nominal democracies can behave less similarly than a democracy and a monarchy in some particular subsystem.

